$\mathrm{SnO}_{2}$ reacts with acids as well as bases to form corresponding salts. So it is an amphoteric oxide. $\begin{array}{l} \mathrm{SnO}_{2}+4 \mathrm{HCl} \rightarrow \mathrm{SnCl}_{4}+2 \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}\\
\mathrm{SnO}_{2}+2 \mathrm{NaOH} \rightarrow \underset{\text{ sod.stannate }}{\mathrm{Na}_{2} \mathrm{SnO}_{3}}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}
\end{array}$
